utbound connection to cloakbrowser.dev is slow, not inbound. So downloading on the server should work if I just give it more time.\n\nThe Chrome binary download is actually working on the server, it just needs more time. Let me try a longer background download.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the situation - the download timed out after 5 minutes. The user wants to know if they can download on their local machine and send it to me. The answer is yes, but the file is very large (500MB+), so transferring it would be slow.\n\nI think the best approach is to just increase the timeout and try the download again on the server directly. CloakBrowser downloads from `https://cloakbrowser.dev/chromium-v146.0.7680.177.3/cloakbrowser-linux-x64.tar.gz` and falls back to GitHub. The issue might just be slow network speed rather than a complete block, so with a proper timeout setting it should complete.","thinkingSignature":"0f122eee2ddb40b1c7b8829b3489b0f16abea8619b911765794604df9a5e303f"},{"type":"text","text":"可以！让我先查清楚需要下载什么文件：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_84smtbcg0kya_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom cloakbrowser.config import get_download_url, get_fallback_download_url, get_archive_name, get_chromium_version, get_platform_tag\n\nversion = get_chromium_version()\ntag = get_platform_tag()\nprint('Platform tag:', tag)\nprint('Chromium version:', version)\nprint('Archive name:', get_archive_name())\nprint()\nprint('Primary URL:', get_download_url())\nprint('GitHub URL:', get_fallback_download_url())\n\"","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":53062,"output":770,"cacheRead":18026,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":71858,"cost":{"input":0.015918599999999998,"output":0.0009239999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0010815599999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.017924159999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778298012468,"responseId":"064ddf9ca5dbd28ff116f8bd5d8b765f"}}
